# npm falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, and .gitignore
# excludes exactly the two things the published package MUST carry:
#
#   packages/dynamic-workflow/dist/          the built engine
#   packages/dynamic-workflow-runtime/dist/  the built harness
#   packages/dynamic-workflow/src/compiler/libs.generated.ts
#
# The vendored sources are committed, but the built output is a build
# artifact (gitignored) that `npm run build` produces. A tarball without it
# installs a plugin that cannot import its own engine.
#
# This file exists so npm uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore. Everything shipped is
# whitelisted by package.json's "files" field; nothing is excluded here.
#
# The build itself is reproduced on install from a git checkout (npm runs
# "prepare" there). A tarball installed from the registry carries the built
# output directly.
